{
  "as_of": "2026-09-27",
  "scope": "Response Content-Digest header admission and exact-content SHA-256/SHA-512 verification before MCP delivery, with the Go streaming transport also verifying at EOF. Local tests use simulated peers and loopback sockets; no deployment.",
  "changes": [
    "Parse RFC 9530 response Content-Digest using its RFC 8941 dictionary, byte-sequence and opaque bare-parameter types before normalization; preserve repeated field values.",
    "Require at least one supported strong algorithm when the field is present; validate known output lengths, reject duplicate algorithm keys and require every supported declared digest to match.",
    "Hash unchanged content after transfer decoding, including partial content and the full multipart envelope; bodyless and interim responses use empty content. MIME part metadata remains separate.",
    "Validate in both full-body/MCP paths. The Go transport additionally maintains bounded incremental hashes and a sticky integrity failure at EOF. Rejected consumed content remains charged.",
    "Protect Content-Digest against Connection nomination and retain all repeated values in Python tool output, including case variants.",
    "Support 1024 dictionary members and 256 parameters per member within existing header byte/field ceilings. Unknown algorithms and parameters are not used as integrity evidence.",
    "No new Snort SID is added."
  ],
