  "limitations": [
    "An unsigned digest does not authenticate its sender or establish safe content, authorization, or protection from every unknown attack; a malicious sender can recompute or omit an optional digest.",
    "This change does not validate outbound request digest fields, Repr-Digest, digest preference fields, legacy Digest, or HTTP Message Signatures.",
    "This is the RFC 9530 response-field profile, not a generic Structured Fields implementation. Existing ASCII, per-field and total-header byte limits still apply; Date/display-string parameter types are outside the referenced RFC 8941.",
    "Trailers and content codings remain excluded by the existing transport profile. MIME part fields are not treated as HTTP message Content-Digest.",
    "Go streaming embedders must discard previously read bytes if EOF validation fails. MCP validates the complete bounded content before exposing it; its backstop may hash content again after the default Go transport.",
    "Full W3C/RFC coverage, external sandbox route enforcement, atomic admission revocation and universal zero-day prevention remain unproved."
  ],
